    "lawCode": "Amd §8, Chap 563 of 2008",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3807A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend chapter 563 of the laws of 2008 amending the education law\nand the public health law relating to immunizing agents to be\nadministered to adults by pharmacists, in relation to extending the\nexpiration of such provisions\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo extend the sunset provision of chapter 563 of the laws\nof 2008 relating to pharmacists.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 amends the effective date provision\nof chapter 563 of the laws of 2008 to from March 31, 2012 to\nMarch 31, 2016.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis bill is intended to improve health results in New\nYork State, by allowing pharmacists to continue to administer\nvaccinations. Chapter 563 of 2008 allows pharmacists, after receiving\nproper training and certification by the Department of Education, to\nadminister vaccines for flu and pneumococcal to adults.\nThis authority is set to expire in March of2012. This bill extends\nthis authority - which is granted in 48 other states to March of 2016.\n\nIn the two years since NYS provided such authority to pharmacists,\nimmunization rates have risen dramatically.\nSince implementation in the fall of 2008, more than 5,000 NYS licensed\npharmacists completed certification requirements and estimates\nsuggest that pharmacists have administered more than one million\nimmunizations in New York in the past twelve months.\n\nClearly, this initiative has been successful by any measure and the\nsunset should therefore be extended.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNone.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n\n",
